{
 "about": "The pose bank for far soldiers (the true-scale plan, SO1). Each pose is a clip at a phase (0 to 1 of that clip's `long`), baked once per soldier file when a battle loads: the file's own skinning (its `about`), keys blended linearly. A far man playing clip C at time t shows pose cycles[C][round(n * (t mod long) / long) mod n] for a loop (n = len(cycles[C])), and for a one-shot clip the nearest phase, the last one once he is past it. A clip not in `cycles` shows the cycle of `instead[C]`, and a clip the file lacks is left out of its bake and also goes by `instead`. Falls are not in the bank: a far man's fall plays as today (skinned), then he is frozen in its last pose. Pose-bank men fire no clip flashes (SO3): their clips' `muzzle_flash` events are skipped; their rounds, if the recording has them, flash as the battle's distance cap allows. Bake cost measured by pose_bank.py --bake (numpy, one core): see `bake_ms`.",
